WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Look at a face upside down, and a strange change can seem ordinary.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Turn the whole image upright. Suddenly, the eyes and mouth may look wrong.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The picture has not changed. Your perception of the features has.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Researchers call this the Thatcher illusion. Later studies found related effects beyond faces, and showed why simple explanations need testing.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.000
It is a story about visual context, not proof that an audio product rewires a brain.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the evidence, try a free twelve-minute focus exercise, and choose deliberately.
